# systemd --user units enabled on caesar. Timers, not their services: the timer pulls the
# service in, and enabling a oneshot service directly would run it at every login.
backup-daily.timer
backup-legal-to-nas.timer
subget-sync.timer
# Irides re-themes the RGB devices, whose colors live in device RAM only (Irides ADR-0003).
# The exception to the rule above, on purpose: this oneshot is enabled so that it runs at
# every login, for the devices that came up in their firmware effect at boot. Irides' udev
# rule (./copies) starts the same unit when a device reappears -- the USB switch. Installed
# by Irides' `make install`; `not found` here means that checkout predates it: rerun it.
irides-lighting.service
